# state: returning   (composed from the kept profile's survey shots; lane.zetaroutes1012)
# Buffy the Vampire Slayer (45410012), Nova, kept profile golden c6b6ec3cb8be.
# Boot and menu cadence read from the survey run z-1791804165-fpsbelow1012-3514899
# (survey.route, HAKUX_ZETA_D24=1); table in docs/lanes/zetaroutes1012/NOTES.md
# section 1. That run's own START/A spam (5s cadence, the same cadence
# buffy.route's first-run menu already uses) produced this screen sequence:
#   052457-booted: title card, "Press START".
#   052502 (START): in-engine cutscene (Giles + fog, ghostly Buffy).
#   052509 (A): main menu (Start Game / Load Game / Options / Extras).
#   052515 (START, Start Game highlighted): "Launch a New Game ... called
#     Buffy 2" / Free Blocks / CONFIRM -- the same confirm screen
#     buffy.route's own comment documents for "Buffy 1" on an empty disk;
#     only the save-slot number differs, because this disk already holds a
#     save. Nothing on the disk is remade or deleted by it.
#   052521 (A): Difficulty select, Easy highlighted.
#   052527 (START): "Summoning" (loading).
#   052532 (A): mission card, "Spanish Mission, Outskirts of Sunnydale,
#     Sunday 11:53PM".
#   052538 (START): live play, canyon, HUD, "Move the R thumbstick..." tip.
# So the menu path below is buffy.route's own (screen-identical on this
# kept-profile disk).
#
# The play loop below is NOT buffy.route's own run-and-jump pattern. A run
# of this route with that pattern (z-1791817586-lane.zetaroutes1012-2316443,
# switch on) reached the mark cleanly (fps_ok=1.0, gameplay=777.6s) but
# failed title_verdict.py's static-window check (static_frac=0.229, bar
# 0.20): route-frames show Buffy running face-first into the canyon's wall
# within ~20s of the mark (083219-play.png on) and pinned there, still
# running in place, through the run's last frame (084448-play.png).
# buffy.route's loop holds LY min continuously for 7+ seconds before its
# first turn (axis LX max at the 8.1s mark) -- too long a straight run for
# this canyon's geometry. spikeout.returning.route's confirmed-working loop
# (nav.py, Thor, 2026-09-27) instead pulses LY for 1s at a time between
# turns and backs off (axis LY max) rather than holding forward through a
# collision. The loop below uses that same pulse-and-vary pattern: a 1s
# forward pulse, a turn or a backward pulse, repeated with the turn
# direction and jump/attack presses varied every cycle so no single
# direction is held long enough to pin Buffy against one piece of geometry.
wait 20
shot boot20
wait 20
shot boot40
wait 20
shot booted
repeat 5 {
    press START
    wait 5
    shot menu-start
    press A
    wait 5
    shot menu-a
}
wait 3
shot pre-mark
mark gameplay               # CHECK: the canyon with the HUD, no PAUSE panel
repeat forever {
    axis LY min
    wait 1
    axis LY mid
    press B
    wait 0.5
    axis LX max
    wait 1
    axis LX mid
    axis LY min
    wait 1
    axis LY mid
    press B
    wait 0.5
    press A
    wait 0.3
    axis LX min
    wait 1
    axis LX mid
    axis LY min
    wait 1
    axis LY mid
    press X
    wait 0.3
    axis LY max
    wait 0.8
    axis LY mid
    press B
    wait 0.5
    shot play
}
